---
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description = 'The terms that apply when you use the GlideLingo website and applications.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service — GlideLingo" description={description} canonicalPath="/terms/">
  <SiteHeader />

  <main id="main-content" class="legal-page shell">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p>Effective September 2, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <article class="legal-copy">
      <p>
        These Terms of Service (“Terms”) govern your use of the GlideLingo website and applications.
        By using GlideLingo, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the service.
      </p>

      <h2>Eligibility and accounts</h2>
      <p>
        You must be legally able to agree to these Terms. You are responsible for the accuracy of your
        account information, activity under your account, and protecting access to your devices and
        sign-in methods. Email <a href="mailto:stefanoscodes26@gmail.com">stefanoscodes26@gmail.com</a> if
        you believe your account has been compromised.
      </p>

      <h2>License to use GlideLingo</h2>
      <p>
        We grant you a limited, personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to install
        and use GlideLingo for language learning, subject to these Terms. GlideLingo and its content,
        design, software, and trademarks remain owned by us or our licensors.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You may not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>break the law, infringe others’ rights, or submit harmful or deceptive content;</li>
        <li>interfere with, overload, probe, or bypass the security of GlideLingo;</li>
        <li>reverse engineer or redistribute the service except where applicable law allows it;</li>
        <li>use automated means to extract content or create competing datasets or services; or</li>
        <li>share, resell, or misuse paid access or another person’s account.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Subscriptions and billing</h2>
      <p>
        GlideLingo may offer free and paid features. The current Pro plan price and billing interval are
        shown before purchase. Subscriptions renew automatically until canceled. You can cancel through
        the billing-management link provided in GlideLingo; cancellation normally takes effect at the end
        of the current paid period. Payments are processed through RevenueCat and its payment provider,
        Stripe. Taxes, refunds, trials, and payment disputes are handled as disclosed at checkout and as
        required by applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>Learning and AI features</h2>
      <p>
        GlideLingo is an educational aid, not a guaranteed path to fluency or a substitute for professional
        translation, legal, medical, immigration, or other expert advice. AI-generated responses and
        feedback can be incomplete or incorrect. Review important information independently and do not
        rely on GlideLingo in safety-critical situations.
      </p>

      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        You retain ownership of content you submit. You give us a limited license to process that content
        only as needed to operate, secure, and improve the features you choose to use. Do not submit content
        you do not have the right to use. Our handling of personal information is described in the
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        GlideLingo relies on third-party identity, hosting, payment, and AI services. Their terms may also
        apply to your use of those services. We are not responsible for third-party services outside our control.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may improve, change, suspend, or discontinue features. We aim to keep GlideLingo available but
        do not promise uninterrupted or error-free operation. We may restrict or terminate access when
        necessary to protect users, enforce these Terms, comply with law, or prevent misuse.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimers and liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, GlideLingo is provided “as is” and “as available,” without
        warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. To the fullest
        extent permitted by law, we will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or
        punitive damages, or for lost data, profits, or opportunities. Nothing in these Terms limits rights or
        liability that applicable law does not allow us to limit.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms. Continued use after an update becomes effective means you accept the
        revised Terms, except where additional consent is required. Questions can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:stefanoscodes26@gmail.com">stefanoscodes26@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
